  FINDING: read the inert-head column. Three `.7` files carry inert heads —
  4.1.7, 4.3.7, 4.5.7, the `(d trig)^m (a+b (c F)^n)^p` family — and they are all
  in section 4. The other files numbered `.7` (4.7.7, 5.3.7, 6.7.7, 7.3.7) are a
  DIFFERENT family (`F^(c(a+b x)) trig(d+e x)^n` and the inverse miscellanies), use
  no inert head, and are not what the corpus's 6.x.7 files mirror.
  The corpus mirrors the inert three as 4.1.7 ... 4.6.7 AND as 6.1.7 ... 6.6.7:
  the same rules serve both, the hyperbolic side via the bridge. Note Rubi has only
  three of them against the corpus's six — sin/tan/sec carry cos/cot/csc, as the
  4.1.0.x and 4.7.x normalization files do for the rest of section 4.

